// @test: https client - TLS-secured HTTP GET against a local TLS server
// @description: A worker thread stands up a TLS server (in-line PEM cert/key)
//   that answers a request over TLS, while the client fetches it via
//   https_get_full by a resolvable hostname (localhost) and validates the
//   parsed status, reason, Content-Length, and body - proving the https module
//   layers network + tls + http cleanly AND that the unverified client resolves
//   hostnames before connecting (#188). The round-trip runs inside
//   https_selfhost so the test needs only one import.
// @category: modules, https, tls, http, network, threads, stdlib
// @expect: pass
// @expect-output: ok
// @expect-return: 0
// @env: VYB_STDLIB=stdlib

